{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>As Elohim caused me to wander.</b> When Nimrod and his companions, the judges of the land, banished me, and I was forced to wander like a lost sheep, hither and thither, away from my father's house, because I shattered the idols and killed Amraphel and his companions. <b>And I said to her</b> etc." "<b>[Say of me.</b> Say about me, he is my brother — which, according to the needs of the hour, it is permissible to change the wording]."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:03.875883824Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}